metadata target.\\n\\nLibrary Preparation Preflight:\\nLibrary preparation preflight did not request additional setup. Summary: msal4j is a token-acquisition SDK (client-credentials, auth-code, device-code, ROPC flows) used entirely in-process. Its own upstream test suite (v1.15.0 pom) tests via Mockito-mocked HTTP interactions and builder/config assertions, not live Azure AD calls or containers. The already-shipped com.azure:azure-identity tests, which wrap msal4j for the same token-acquisition purpose, follow the identical pattern in this repo — self-contained builder/credential-chaining tests with no Docker image or extra Maven dependency, only the default assertj/junit scaffold.\\n\\nRules (test contract: §root/FS-test-contract):\\n- The binding test contract is `docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md` in this\\n  repository. Read it in full before writing any test and follow all of it.\\n- Write tests in `Java` under the module's existing `src/test/java` tree.\\n- Don't duplicate tested features.\\n- Modify only the test file. Update build.gradle only to add missing classpath dependencies (§root/FS-test-contract.3.4) or configuration within the bounds of §root/FS-test-contract.2.7.\\n- You may inspect the repository only to learn local test style and structure.\\n- If you are unsure about the library's API, look it up on the internet.\\n- Do not compile, run, or verify tests yourself. The workflow will do that externally.\\n- Reporter issue context identifies what is missing; infer the relevant public API paths from that context and cover them in tests. §root/FS-test-contract.1.5\\n\"}], \"timestamp\": 1790132721293}}\n[recv] {\"type\": \"message_start\", \"message\": {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [], \"api\": \"openai-codex-responses\", \"provider\": \"openai-codex\", \"model\": \"gpt-5.6-sol\", \"usage\": {\"input\": 0, \"output\": 0, \"cacheRead\": 0, \"cacheWrite\": 0, \"totalTokens\": 0, \"cost\": {\"input\": 0, \"output\": 0, \"cacheRead\": 0, \"c