tadata target.\\n\\nLibrary Preparation Preflight:\\nLibrary preparation preflight did not request additional setup. Summary: msal4j is a token-acquisition SDK (client-credentials, auth-code, device-code, ROPC flows) used entirely in-process. Its own upstream test suite (v1.15.0 pom) tests via Mockito-mocked HTTP interactions and builder/config assertions, not live Azure AD calls or containers. The already-shipped com.azure:azure-identity tests, which wrap msal4j for the same token-acquisition purpose, follow the identical pattern in this repo — self-contained builder/credential-chaining tests with no Docker image or extra Maven dependency, only the default assertj/junit scaffold.\\n\\nRules (test contract: §root/FS-test-contract):\\n- The binding test contract is `docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md` in this\\n  repository. Read it in full before writing any test and follow all of it.\\n- Write tests in `Java` under the module's existing `src/test/java` tree.\\n- Don't duplicate tested features.\\n- Modify only the test file. Update build.gradle only to add missing classpath dependencies (§root/FS-test-contract.3.4) or configuration within the bounds of §root/FS-test-contract.2.7.\\n- You may inspect the repository only to learn local test style and structure.\\n- If you are unsure about the library's API, look it up on the internet.\\n- Do not compile, run, or verify tests yourself. The workflow will do that externally.\\n- Reporter issue context identifies what is missing; infer the relevant public API paths from that context and cover them in tests. §root/FS-test-contract.1.5\\n\"}], \"timestamp\": 1790132721293}}\n[recv] {\"type\": \"message_start\", \"message\": {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [], \"api\": \"openai-codex-responses\", \"provider\": \"openai-codex\", \"model\": \"gpt-5.6-sol\", \"usage\": {\"input\": 0, \"output\": 0, \"cacheRead\": 0, \"cacheWrite\": 0, \"totalTokens\": 0, \"cost\": {\"input\": 0, \"output\": 0, \"cacheRead\": 0, \"cacheWrite\": 0, \"total\": 0}}, \"stopReason\": \"pending\", \"timestamp\": 1790132721304}}\n[assistant-event] thinking_start\n[thinking] **Inspecting project docs and test requirements**\n[thinking] \n[thinking] **Listing project root files for context**\n[thinking] \n[assistant-event] thinking_end\n[tool-call] start id=unknown\n[tool-call] delta {\"path\":\"README.md\"}\n[tool-call] end id=call_y7xdszaEyeTFHY9OJdlENF0B|fc_00d0dceb5122f70c016ab341fa434c87d2a2437a1d0d693668 name=read args={\"path\": \"README.md\"}\n[tool-call] start id=unknown\n[tool-call] delta {\"path\":\"DEVELOPING.md\"}\n[tool-call] end id=call_G1RCDtuxw1RTZcPQZO67NHM3|fc_00d0dceb5122f70c016ab341fa436087d2b71b2a2652e79663 name=read args={\"path\": \"DEVELOPING.md\"}\n[tool-call] start id=unknown\n[tool-call] delta {\"path\":\"docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md\"}\n[tool-call] end id=call_3mTFukaXRUGzNvoMTRs61w91|fc_00d0dceb5122f70c016ab341fa436887d29ff500b1d07550cd name=read args={\"path\": \"docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md\"}\n[tool-call] start id=unknown\n[tool-call] delta {\"path\":\"docs/README.md\"}\n[tool-call] end id=call_iQU5PDjLeyRVtOUDseyiXG4f|fc_00d0dceb5122f70c016ab341fa437087d2b1a97ef6ab6a89f3 name=read args={\"path\": \"docs/README.md\"}\n[recv] {\"type\": \"message_end\", \"message\": {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [{\"type\": \"thinking\", \"thinking\": \"**Inspecting project docs and test requirements**\\n\\n**Listing project root files for context**\", \"thinkingSignature\": \"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"rs_00d0dceb5122f70c016ab341f2fcac87d2953c27219dd41ec6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"reasoning\\\",\\\"content\\\":[],\\\"encrypted_content\\\":\\\"gAAAAABqs0H6MQ057N7l3TubVmTIHR7oztqzQc7SLnA467-Ydgo8pwjVX-eUWbR9WpNYtF0Kt37mF_r-dhVHdmgPairUZTABphdiadtkrUMU2K0n1pZ_MatQbkUdkQQHKsybTxQQO6zy3WPJ7D5pHpk_DBBtA3eiUo1Tx4sN2ExGCJXdbv2fqcUAatbjDgb5lr4i0fKIArGjskID2b0nV2mAL20rWtZgFeZDBcMW0wlaOmkPNZ_GO-i9YW7PAVFNJTgy-Jh7RQIYsdvOt0uDH2IsKIKad9acccbJUDCSTrw8IdsWsFwRX98BT2YEQsP_bNtPFLyczXhWy4RGkbFLO