meta%2Fhuman-intervention%2Fissue-10067-library-new-request-com.microsoft.azure-msal4j-1.15.0-fa2117c4.\n\nThe most likely failing stage is dynamic-access reporting or the subsequent publication handoff, not test execution. `human-intervention-logs/com.microsoft.azure:msal4j:1.15.0/dynamic-access-report/generateDynamicAccessCoverageReport-2026-09-23T04-38-26-972619Z.log` reports that `nativeTestCompile/dynamic-access` was not produced and fails rather than creating an ambiguous empty report. The same failure appears in `human-intervention-logs/com.microsoft.azure:msal4j:1.15.0/gradle/generateDynamicAccessCoverageReport-2026-09-23T05-06-32-894895Z.log`.\n\nLater evidence shows the generated work itself completed successfully: `human-intervention-logs/com.microsoft.azure:msal4j:1.15.0/gradle-test/gradle-test-2026-09-23T05-26-50-072812Z.log` records all 10 native tests passing, while metadata validation, Checkstyle, Spotless, and statistics generation also pass. The preserved `execution-metrics.json` records success with 435 generated lines and 38.45% code coverage, but incorrectly represents the unavailable dynamic-access data as 0/0; no publication descriptor was produced for this coordinate.\n\nManual next steps:\n\n1. Cleanly rebuild the trace-enabled native test and determine why `-H:TrackDynamicAccess` creates no `dynamic-access` output directory, then rerun `generateDynamicAccessCoverageReport`.\n2. Revalidate the preserved branch with coordinate-scoped index, metadata, and full test tasks, confirming the 10 JVM/native tests remain green.\n3. Regenerate stats and publication data from a real dynamic-access result, avoiding conversion of unavailable coverage into a synthetic 0/0 result, then resume publication.", "textSignature": "{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0aed6916d99a7bbe016ab36482e09487d2a8cd1c34ebd64ad3\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}], "api": "openai-codex-responses", "provider": "openai-codex", "model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "usage": {"input": 19773, "output": 991, "ca